ITR.LEGEND=> flow, X exchange, , list separator, ${} expansion, | item separator, CRITICAL severity marker, MAJOR severity marker, CU computational unit, -> relation arrow
ARCH=HEX,DI,DIP,NO_CROSS_LAYER,PORT_FLOW_OUT_IN,DOTENV_WALKUP,CODER_FEEDBACK,SEVERITY,ITR_LIFECYCLE,HARD_FAIL,DTR_DELTA_VERIFICATION
LAYER.ORDER=DOMAIN,APPLICATION,INFRASTRUCTURE,CONTROL
APP=commit-tool
ITERATION=002
SEVERITY_BASELINE=CRITICAL
SCOPE=Correct spec deviations from ITERATION=001: fix build.sbt assembly script (MAJOR), fix body truncation in CommitMessage.fromRaw (MINOR), fix single-quote ${} expansion in DotEnvLoader (MINOR), add ReadError type for IO errors, update tests

#
# Baseline: previous implementation is at HEAD
# This ITERATION targets only the listed fixes
#

CU.1.ADDRESS=commit-tool/build.sbt
CU.1.LABEL=SEVERITY:MAJOR — Fix assembly prepend script: replace defaultUniversalScript with explicit script per spec
CU.1.INSTRUCT=Replace the assembly configuration block. Remove the assembly / assemblyOption line that uses defaultUniversalScript(shebang = false). Add these lines instead:
  assembly / assemblyJarName := "commit-tool"
  assembly / assemblyOutputPath := baseDirectory.value / "commit-tool"
  assembly / assemblyPrependShellScript := Some(Seq(
    "#!/usr/bin/env sh",
    """exec java -jar "$0" "$@""""
  ))
Keep all other build.sbt content (name, organization, scalaVersion, mainClass, resolvers, scalacOptions, Test/fork, libraryDependencies) unchanged.

CU.2.ADDRESS=commit-tool/src/main/scala/commitool/domain/models/CommitMessage.scala
CU.2.LABEL=SEVERITY:MINOR — Fix body truncation: body must be ALL content after the header-blank-line separator, preserving internal blank lines
CU.2.INSTRUCT=In the fromRaw companion object method, replace the body extraction logic (lines ~35-45 of current file) with:
  val bodyStartIndex = raw.indexOf("\n\n")
  val bodyContent = if (bodyStartIndex != -1) {
    raw.substring(bodyStartIndex + 2).trim
  } else ""
  Then validate bodyContent.nonEmpty -> Left(EmptyBody), else use it as-is.
  Remove the logic that searches for firstBlankLineIndex within bodyLines and truncates there. The body should preserve all content, including any blank lines within it, after the first \n\n separator.
  Also verify the test at CommitMessageSpec handles multi-paragraph bodies (body with internal blank lines) correctly.

CU.3.ADDRESS=commit-tool/src/main/scala/commitool/infrastructure/environment/DotEnvLoader.scala
CU.3.LABEL=SEVERITY:MINOR — Fix single-quoted value expansion: literal values must NOT undergo ${} expansion
CU.3.INSTRUCT=Modify the parsing pipeline to tag values by their quoting mode:
  1. Define a private sealed trait ValueType with case classes Literal(value: String) and Expandable(value: String)
  2. Change parseValue to return ValueType instead of String:
     - Single-quoted ('...') -> Literal(content inside quotes, with quotes stripped)
     - Double-quoted ("...") -> Expandable(content inside quotes, with quotes stripped)
     - Unquoted -> Expandable(value.trim)
  3. Update the keyValueRegex handler in load() to store ValueType instead of raw String.
     Keep mutable Map[String, ValueType] for intermediate storage.
  4. In resolveExpansions (or in a post-processing step after resolution), skip expansion for Literal values:
     - Expandable values: apply varExpansionRegex replacement as before
     - Literal values: return the value as-is, no expansion
  5. Remove the dead-code sys.env.foreach block on the immutable map (currently lines 36-38) — system env vars are already loaded before .env processing.
  Ensure the final return Map[String, String] contains only the resolved string values.

CU.4.ADDRESS=commit-tool/src/main/scala/commitool/domain/models/CommitValidationError.scala
CU.4.LABEL=SEVERITY:TRIVIAL — Add ReadError case for file IO errors (currently misusing GitError)
CU.4.INSTRUCT=Add a new case class:
  case class ReadError(path: String, detail: String) extends CommitValidationError {
    override def message: String = s"Error reading file '$path': $detail"
  }
  Keep all existing error types unchanged.

CU.5.ADDRESS=commit-tool/src/main/scala/commitool/infrastructure/adapter/FileSystemContentReader.scala
CU.5.LABEL=SEVERITY:TRIVIAL — Use ReadError instead of GitError for IOException
CU.5.INSTRUCT=Replace the two catch blocks that use `CommitValidationError.GitError(...)` for file IO errors:
  - `case e: IOException => Left(ReadError(path, e.getMessage))`
  - `case NonFatal(e) => Left(ReadError(path, e.getMessage))`
  Remove the GitError import if it's no longer needed (but keep it if still referenced elsewhere in the file).
  Add import for ReadError if not already present.

CU.6.ADDRESS=commit-tool/src/test/scala/commitool/domain/models/CommitMessageSpec.scala
CU.6.LABEL=Add test for multi-paragraph body (with internal blank lines) to verify body truncation fix
CU.6.INSTRUCT=Add a test case:
  it should "preserve multi-paragraph body with blank lines" in {
    val raw = "feat(scope): description\n\nParagraph one.\n\nParagraph two.\n\nParagraph three."
    CommitMessage.fromRaw(raw) should matchPattern {
      case Right(CommitMessage(_, _, _, body)) if body == "Paragraph one.\n\nParagraph two.\n\nParagraph three." =>
    }
  }
CU.6.DEPENDENCY=CU.2

CU.7.ADDRESS=commit-tool/src/test/scala/commitool/domain/models/CommitTypeSpec.scala
CU.7.LABEL=Tests already exist — no change needed
CU.7.INSTRUCT=No action required. Acknowledged.

